content.text:
Done. The live server at `http://localhost:4000/publications/` now shows the workshop badges.

## What I changed

1. **`_bibliography/mine.bib`** — added `workshop={true}` to the five workshop papers:
   - Learned Relay Representations (ICML FoGen Workshop)
   - Improved Sampling from Masked Diffusion Models (NeurIPS SPIGM Workshop)
   - Insertion Language Models (NeurIPS SPIGM Workshop)
   - Weakly Supervised Medication Regimen Extraction (Clinical NLP Workshop)
   - Reading Comprehension as NLI (StarSem Workshop at COLING)

2. **`_layouts/bib.html`** — renders a `Workshop` badge right after the venue badge whenever `entry.workshop` is set:

```15:25:_layouts/bib.html
      {%- else -%}
      <abbr class="badge">{{entry.abbr}}</abbr>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if entry.workshop -%}
      <abbr class="badge workshop">Workshop</abbr>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
```

3. **`_sass/_base.scss`** — styled the workshop badge as an outlined badge (transparent background, theme-color border/text) so it reads as a secondary tag next to the solid venue badge:

```684:689:_sass/_base.scss
        abbr.workshop {
          background-color: transparent !important;
          color: var(--global-theme-color);
          border: 1px solid var(--global-theme-color);
          margin-left: 0.4rem;
        }
```

4. **`_config.yml`** — added `workshop` (and `conferenceshort`, which was previously unfiltered) to `filtered_bibtex_keywords` so these custom fields don't leak into the exported BibTeX shown via the "Bib" button.

One note: the running Jekyll server had a pre-existing UTF-8 locale crash when converting a Jupyter notebook (`invalid byte sequence in US-ASCII`). I restarted it with `LC_ALL=en_US.UTF-8` set so the build completes cleanly. If you launch `jekyll serve` yourself, you may want that locale exported in your shell profile to avoid that error.

Want me to use a different look for the badge (e.g., a filled gray pill, or smaller text) instead of the outlined style?

